{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790291619,"nonce":"bY7PsTZHTp54doFSo7cxVTIPiMA=","title":"wasm32: std::time clocks panic inside Module.run","message":"CI \"wasm headless-chrome smoke\" failed at the Node smoke on every push since 2026-09-18: `run()` panics with \"time not implemented on this platform\" (std/src/sys/time/unsupported.rs). Reproduced locally at 678f49eb: `./build.sh node \u0026\u0026 node test/node_smoke.mjs`.\n\nCause: `std::time::Instant::now()` on the interpreter path. The first hit is hir_interp.rs's first-call body timer (`started = Instant::now()` around `body_source`), which runs on every first call even with the phase trace off. Other std clocks compiled into the wasm32 build: drop_insert.rs (run_module timers), lowering.rs (per-phase timer), tiered_backend.rs, cranelift_backend.rs, llvm_jit_backend.rs; zyntax_embed import_chain.rs, snapshot.rs, lower.rs, interp_runtime.rs, runtime/classic.rs, runtime/tiered.rs; zrtl async_support.rs (block_on timeouts, Timer).\n\nFix: every one of them uses web_time (std::time on native, performance.now() on wasm32). zrtl gains the web-time dependency.\n\nGuard: native clippy cannot see the difference, because web_time::Instant is std::time::Instant on native. The wasm job now runs `cargo clippy -p zyntax_wasm --lib --target wasm32-unknown-unknown` with CLIPPY_CONF_DIR=crates/zyntax_wasm/clippy-wasm32, whose clippy.toml disallows std::time::Instant / SystemTime (types and ::now). That lints zyntax_wasm and every workspace crate it links (compiler, embed, zrtl, passes, typed_ast, zyn_peg). Verified at 678f49eb: it reports all 24 sites and fails.","files":null}]}